+# S004 Data Model: Provider retry quota
+
+## Scope
+
+This model is the durable accounting boundary for S004. It is intentionally storage-neutral; implementation must translate it into the repository’s established schema and migration conventions.
+
+## Entities
+
+### WorkspaceRetryQuota
+
+One row per workspace whose retries are quota-controlled.
+
+| Field | Type | Rules |
+|-------|------|-------|
+| `workspace_id` | stable workspace identifier | Primary key; derived from the retry attempt, never trusted from a callback payload. |
+| `available_credits` | non-negative integer | `>= 0`; decremented only by a successful conditional reservation and incremented only by a successful restore transition. |
+| `updated_at` | timestamp | Updated in the same transaction as each balance mutation. |
+
+### RetryCreditReservation
+
+One durable record for the quota decision of a retry attempt.
+
+| Field | Type | Rules |
+|-------|------|-------|
+| `reservation_id` | stable identifier | Primary key; returned internally to the dispatcher. |
+| `workspace_id` | stable workspace identifier | Foreign key/logical reference to `WorkspaceRetryQuota`. |
+| `retry_attempt_id` | stable identifier | Unique; makes duplicate start commands return the existing reservation rather than reserve again. |
+| `provider_delivery_id` | nullable stable identifier | Unique when present; binds authenticated provider callbacks to one reservation. |
+| `state` | enum | `reserved`, `finalized`, or `restored`. |
+| `terminal_reason` | nullable enum/text | Required for `restored`: `provider_failed`, `provider_timed_out`, or `cancelled`; optional audit detail for `finalized`. |
+| `reserved_at` | timestamp | Set on initial successful reservation. |
+| `terminal_at` | nullable timestamp | Set exactly once when leaving `reserved`. |
+| `callback_idempotency_key` | nullable stable identifier | Persisted when applicable; unique or deduplicated within the reservation to make repeated callback delivery harmless. |
+
+## Relationships
+
+```text
+WorkspaceRetryQuota (1) ──── (many) RetryCreditReservation
+                 workspace_id        workspace_id
+```
+
+Each reservation belongs to exactly one workspace. A retry attempt has at most one reservation, and a provider delivery/callback maps to at most one reservation.
+
+## State Machine
+
+```text
+                 provider accepted
+reserved ─────────────────────────► finalized
+   │
+   ├── provider failed
+   ├── provider timed out
+   └── cancelled
+                 │
+                 ▼
+              restored
+```
+
+`finalized` and `restored` are terminal. Any later duplicate or conflicting callback returns the persisted terminal outcome and changes neither reservation nor quota.
+
+## Transactional Operations and Invariants
+
+### Reserve
+
+Within one transaction:
+
+1. Return the existing reservation if `retry_attempt_id` already exists.
+2. Otherwise conditionally decrement the workspace quota only when `available_credits > 0`.
+3. If the decrement affected one row, insert the `reserved` reservation and commit.
+4. If no row was affected, reject as quota exhausted and do not call the provider.
+
+### Finalize
+
+Within one transaction, update a matching `reserved` reservation to `finalized`. The update predicate includes the reservation identity and `state = reserved`. If no row matches, return the existing terminal outcome; do not mutate quota.
+
+### Restore
+
+Within one transaction:
+
+1. Update a matching `reserved` reservation to `restored` with its terminal reason, guarded by `state = reserved`.
+2. Only if that update changed one row, increment the corresponding workspace quota by one.
+3. Commit both changes together.
+
+## Database Constraints
+
+- `WorkspaceRetryQuota.available_credits >= 0`.
+- Unique `RetryCreditReservation.retry_attempt_id`.
+- Unique non-null `RetryCreditReservation.provider_delivery_id` where provider identity is available.
+- At most one terminal transition per reservation, enforced by state-guarded updates rather than application-level branching alone.
+- A foreign key or equivalent referential invariant from reservation workspace to quota workspace.
+
+## Failure Handling
+
+- If dispatch cannot begin because no credit is available, no reservation is created and the provider is not invoked.
+- If the provider call throws or times out after reservation, the timeout/failure handler applies the same restore operation; retries of that handler are safe.
+- If a process crashes after the provider call but before outcome processing, recovery must reconcile the durable reservation with the provider delivery state before either finalizing or restoring. It must never blindly re-credit an accepted delivery.
+
+---
+
+*Derived solely from S004 acceptance criteria; no existing repository schema was available to refine names or types.*
